    "leftUpperLeg",
    "rightUpperLeg"
  ],
  "usage": "Use for a jump backflip, backward somersault, or salto belakang on the current Rhino rig. Duration is 72 frames at 30 FPS (2.4 seconds). Preserve the body-root hierarchy, local transforms, and unwrapped rotation values through -360 degrees; shortest-angle interpolation or normalizing the final rotation to zero can destroy the full turn. The starting and ending poses are visually equivalent, but the body rotation differs by one full revolution. For repeated playback, wrap directly to frame 0 rather than interpolating from -360 to 0. The source rig has two bones named right_arm: ID 2 is the upper arm (parent ID 1), and ID 3 is the right hand (parent ID 2, carrying sword ID 9). Apply tracks by boneId on this rig; name-only mapping cannot distinguish these tracks. Eyes and sword retain their local transforms and inherit their parents' motion.",
